# [[Feature name]]

> A feature spec cuts vertically through every standards layer. It never overrides a standard —
> an exception needs an ADR — and it never restates one: cite the rule, do not copy it.
>
> Remove a section only by replacing it with `Not applicable — <why>`. An empty section reads as
> "not yet considered", and a later agent will fill it with invention. Mark every gap inline as
> `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: question]`; a spec with any marker left cannot be approved.
>
> Cross-references to a rule use the `docs/`-relative path and the rule number, for example
> `08-reliability/timeouts-retries.md` R3. Never a bare file name.

